--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored components (in vendor/)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

llama-cpp-rs
    Rust bindings over llama.cpp. Licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0.
    License files: vendor/llama-cpp-rs/LICENSE-MIT, vendor/llama-cpp-rs/LICENSE-APACHE.
    The bundled llama.cpp sources under vendor/llama-cpp-rs/llama-cpp-sys-2/llama.cpp
    retain their upstream MIT license and copyright headers.

    Multi-token-prediction speculative decoding comes from
    DINOZYAVIER/llama-cpp-rs branch mtp-speculative-decoding, proposed upstream
    as utilityai/llama-cpp-rs#1027.

    The kimi-k3 architecture (Kimi Delta Attention, gated MLA, latent MoE,
    cross-layer residual attention) is adapted from Piotr Wilkin's
    ggml-org/llama.cpp#26185. The MoonViT-3d vision tower and the kimik3 clip
    projector are adapted from unslothai/llama.cpp branch
    kimi-k3-fullsize-vision, which is also what produced the mmproj GGUF
    published at unsloth/Kimi-K3-GGUF. Both carry llama.cpp's MIT license.

glass_pumpkin
    Cryptographic prime generation. License: vendor/glass_pumpkin/LICENSE.

erc8004-solana
    ERC-8004 reference on Solana. License: vendor/erc8004-solana/LICENSE.

dkls23-core, dkls23-secp256k1
    DKLS23 threshold ECDSA. Vendored under [patch.crates-io] for the bridge
    threshold-signing path.

erc8004-atom, erc8004-daml, erc8004-evm
    ERC-8004 reference material across execution environments.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Principal dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Networking and transport
    libp2p, iroh, iroh-blobs, iroh-gossip, iroh-docs, rustls, aws-lc-rs, quinn

Execution
    revm (EVM)
    solana-svm and the solana-* runtime crates (SVM)
    ndarray, ort (ONNX Runtime), safetensors, tokenizers (inference runtimes)
    llama-cpp-2 (language-model serving)

Consensus and cryptography
    ed25519-dalek, k256, p256, p384, curve25519-dalek, ecdsa, signature
    blst (BLS12-381)
    ml-kem, ml-dsa, slh-dsa (post-quantum, FIPS 203/204/205)
    frost-ed25519, frost-secp256k1 (threshold signatures)
    argon2, aes-gcm, x25519-dalek, sha2, sha3, ripemd, zeroize

Zero-knowledge
    p3-* (Plonky3) STARK stack over the KoalaBear field

Storage and data
    rocksdb, lancedb, tantivy, arrow, tokio-postgres, redis
    reed-solomon-erasure, multihash, cid

Serialization and protocol
    serde, serde_json, bincode, prost, ciborium, rlp, quick-xml

Runtime and utilities
    tokio, futures, async-trait, dashmap, parking_lot, thiserror, anyhow,
    tracing, reqwest, hyper, axum, tower, clap, uuid, chrono

Agent and model-context protocols
    rmcp (Model Context Protocol)

A machine-readable list of every dependency and its resolved version is in
